{"number": 135, "text": "                      Word        stress:       Further        practice\n\n                      This section gives further practice of suffixes covered in Units 11 and 12.\n\n              1       The  suffixes  -able,  -age  and  -al\n                      Write the following words in the table according to their stress pattern:\n                                 =  arrival   assemblage      changeable                  emotional\n                      enjoyable  —  functional _  original               _— percentage\n\n                       Ooo                             000                            0000\n                                                                                      advisable\n\n\n                      Now   listen, check your answers and repeat the words after the recording.\n                      Most  words  with the suffixes -able, -age, and -al have stress on the same syllable as their root\n                      word.  However,  there are exceptions. Can you find the one exception in the words you have\n                      written in the table?\n                A     See Word  stress 7 for words ending\n\n              2       The  suffixes  -ful,  -less and  -ness\n                      Write the following words  in the table according to their stress pattern:\n                                       alertness   assertiveness    awkwardness       characterless   colourless\n                      deviousness  _                  disgraceful    eventful    powerful      regardless\n                       Ooo                     000                    Oooo                    0000\n                                                                                              abrasiveness\n\n\n                      Now   listen, check your answers and repeat the words after the recording.\n                      Words  with the suffixes -ful, -less, and -ness have stress on the same syllable as their root word.\n\